/E (The start of 2026 presents a dual reality for India-Mexico trade. The new tariffs pose an immediate threat to traditional export sectors, demanding a swift and strategic response, primarily through the pursuit of an FTA. Simultaneously, the opportunities in nearshoring, high-potential products \(Pharma, Chemicals\), and the rapidly expanding service sector offer compelling avenues for growth. Indian businesses that adapt quickly by investing in local Mexican presence and focusing on service-based collaboration are best positioned to thrive in this evolving bilateral relationship.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
